 Enterprise-Level CI/CD Deep Dive

GitLab CI/CD is powerful because CI, CD, security, and DevOps live in one platform.
For 2–4 years experience, interviewers expect real pipeline ownership, not just YAML basics.

🔹 GitLab CI/CD Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• What is GitLab CI/CD and how does it work?
• GitLab CI architecture
• What is .gitlab-ci.yml and where is it stored?
• Stages vs Jobs — difference and execution flow
• What are GitLab Runners? (Shared vs Specific)
• How does a runner pick a job?
• What are GitLab CI variables?
• How do you manage secrets securely in GitLab CI?
• What are artifacts and cache?
• Cache vs artifacts — when to use which?
• How do you implement multi-stage pipelines?
• GitLab CI with Docker
• GitLab CI with Kubernetes
• What is GitLab Auto DevOps?
• GitLab CI vs Jenkins vs GitHub Actions
• How do you secure GitLab CI pipelines?
• How do you scale GitLab runners?
• Runner not picking jobs — troubleshooting steps
• Pipeline slow due to Docker image pull — optimization
• Secrets printed in logs — immediate fix
• Different deployments for Dev / QA / Prod — how?
• How do you implement rollback in GitLab CI?
• Pipeline failed in production stage — what next?
• Keep .gitlab-ci.yml clean and modular
• Use cache to speed up pipelines
• Protect variables for production
• Restrict runner permissions
• Use manual jobs for production deployments
• Monitor runners for performance
• Follow least privilege access

Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “We use protected variables, manual approvals, and environment-based deployments in GitLab CI”
you already sound like a solid 2–4 years DevOps engineer.
